VCVTTPH2{,U}DQ / VCVTTPH2{,U}QQ: dispatch to the truncating handlers

The eight packed fp16-to-dword and fp16-to-qword *truncating* rows in the EVEX
opcode table name the truncating instruction but bind the non-truncating
execute method: BX_IA_EVEX_VCVTTPH2DQ_VdqWph points at VCVTPH2DQ_VdqWphR, and
so on through the UDQ, QQ and UQQ forms and each one's _Kmask twin. So
`vcvttph2dq` rounds by the current rounding mode instead of toward zero:
of -367.5 it returns RN's -368, not truncation's -367.

The truncating methods exist and are correct — avx512_cvt16.cc defines all
eight, keyed on f16_to_{i32,ui32,i64,ui64}_round_to_zero — they were simply
never referenced. Nothing else was wrong with the rows: the load functions,
operand kinds, ISA gate and EVEX attributes already match their non-truncating
siblings, and the sibling families that were bound correctly (VCVTTPH2{,U}W,
the scalar VCVTTSH2{,U}SI) show what these should have looked like. A
copy-paste slip in the table, nothing deeper.

The disassembly strings were copied along with the handler, so both of each
row's mnemonics also read "vcvtph2dq". That is why Bochs' own internal disasm
agreed with the wrong result, and it is fixed here too.

Found by this crate's differential suite; see docs/backend-differences.md §4i.
Still present on upstream master as of 2026-08-21 (7cf9830).

The hunks below are deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

